            are in corresppndence with trivializations of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
          %p
            On the other hand we have that
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L X
            correspond to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \mathcal{G}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
          %p
            So we find that in general
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are not in bijection to just all orientations of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L X
